# Field 8 caller chain on the full placed domain (LT11)

The record's caller theorems (`FrontierEntry1591Callers.entry_correct`,
`entry_eq`, `division_step`, and LT6's `hostedExitN_pw`) take the kernel support
premise `wires K ⊆ OB5Support.logicalSites` only to feed the domain-generic
transfer theorems `FrontierEntry1591Callers.entryTransfer` and
`wordTransferN` with an injectivity domain.  `OB5Support.logicalSites` excludes
the record's omitted bank `base 515..716`, so it cannot contain the hosted
kernels of the staircase (slack hosts `base 515..582`, codec scratch).

Here the same transfers are run on `callerDomain` = the 2,314 shared labels
plus the generic control and the three scalar selectors.  On that domain
`wireFn2 L` is injective (it is a sub-domain of the record's placed point
inventory `MappedCompressed.pointIndexSites`), every shared work label is sent
into the clean dialog pool (`MappedCompressed.pointIndexWire_work_mem`), and no
label is sent to the caller's `control` wire (whose only preimage in the placed
inventory is the metadata label `base 2402`).

Proved here (namespace `ECDSAAdd.Entrant.StairSemanticFinal`):
* `callerDomain`, `logical_sub_caller`, `placed_injOn`, `wireFn2_injOn_caller`,
  `sharedWork_caller`, `control_not_caller_image`;
* `entry_correctD`, `entry_eqD`, `division_stepD` (record proofs, domain
  `callerDomain`);
* `hostedEntryRef_stepD`, `hostedStageAll_stepD`, `entryStage_eqD`,
  `hostedExitN_pwD`, `hosted_rest_pwD`, `secondStage_eqD` (LT6's hosted stage
  lemmas with the support premise in `callerDomain`).
