under `FlagTop.rho`, `AboveFieldPointDevelop.middle`, `finiteBorrow`, the
`Wrapper5.U` wrapper) is reused unchanged: the hosted program differs from the
record program only in the two kernels, and every caller theorem sees a kernel
only through the kernel-generic transfers of `StairCallerDomain`.

Compared with LT6's `StairCallerMiddle.semantic_composition_of_field`, whose
placement premise `wires K ⊆ OB5Support.logicalSites` excludes the record's
omitted bank `base 515..716` (and therefore fails for the slack hosts
`base 515..582` and the codec scratch of the current host plan), the premise
here is the support of the hosted kernels in `callerDomain` (the 2,314 shared
point labels plus the generic control and the scalar selectors), which is the
exact injectivity domain of the record placement on shared labels.

Main results (namespace `ECDSAAdd.Entrant.StairSemanticFinal`):
* `semantic_composition_of_supportD` / `semantic_composition_final`
  (from `StairCertificate.HostReplaySpec concreteAssembly`, field 13);
* the premises `EntrySupportD` / `ExitSupportD` are stated directly on the
  hosted kernels `StairHostsSchedule.entryKernel/exitKernel checkpointPrimitives
  hostPlan` (proved for CANON v3 in `StairCallerV3Kernel`).
-/

